{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 8, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS A CLEAR EXAMPLE OF A MORAL ABSOLUTISM, WHICH CAN LEAD TO UNDESIRABLE CONSEQUENCES. IT FAILS TO CONSIDER THE COMPLEXITIES OF SITUATIONS WHERE THE LAW MAY NOT ALWAYS BE JUST OR FAIR, BUT FOLLOWING IT MAY STILL BE THE MOST RESPONSIBLE COURSE OF ACTION. BY TAKING A BINARY APPROACH TO MORAL DILEMMAS, THIS SENTENCE IGNORES THE FACT THAT THE REAL WORLD OFTEN REQUIRES GRAY AREA THINKING AND COMPROMISE.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nANOTHER PROBLEM WITH THIS SENTENCE IS THAT IT PROVIDES NO GUIDANCE ON HOW TO DETERMINE WHETHER A LAW IS \"BAD\" IN THE FIRST PLACE. WHO GETS TO DECIDE WHAT MAKES A LAW BAD, AND BASED ON WHAT CRITERIA? WITHOUT A CLEAR FRAMEWORK FOR ASSESSING THE MORALITY OF A LAW, THIS SENTENCE REDUCES THE COMPLEX ISSUE OF LEGALITY TO A SIMPLE MATTER OF PERSONAL OPINION. THIS LACK OF CLARITY LEAVES THE SENTENCE FEELING VAGUE AND UNHELPFUL, RATHER THAN A USEFUL GUIDE FOR NAVIGATING MORAL DILEMMAS.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -0.0023090388}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -0.00035089056}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -0.000283082}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0047079194}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -4.5299425e-06}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.16702348}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.58440435}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -0.23184392}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": -3.0517112e-05}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.578928}, {"token": "IF", "logprob": -0.0030436642}, {"token": " THE", "logprob": -8.344616e-06}, {"token": " LAW", "logprob": -0.00019369634}, {"token": " IS", "logprob": -3.4331686e-05}, {"token": " BAD", "logprob": -4.9470633e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00059146073}, {"token": " YOU", "logprob": -0.00012623466}, {"token": " SHOULD", "logprob": -0.00040892346}, {"token": " NOT", "logprob": -1.3589766e-05}, {"token": " FOLLOW", "logprob": -9.45285e-05}, {"token"